config/cdn.yaml and config/robots.txt are generated from the third-party sources below.
Each source keeps its own licence. Licences were checked at the source on 2026-11-09.

- OWASP Core Rule Set (https://github.com/coreruleset/coreruleset)
  Copyright 2026 OWASP CRS project. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). CRS ships no NOTICE file.
  Modifications: data lists and regular expressions were converted to AEM CDN
  traffic-filter syntax (case-insensitive matching, argument-boundary anchors,
  '+' treated as space, ARGS rules scoped to the query string). Only a subset of
  rules is used; this is not the CRS and is not endorsed by the OWASP CRS project.

- X4BNet lists_vpn (https://github.com/X4BNet/lists_vpn)
  Copyright (c) 2026 X4B (Mathew Heard). MIT License (stated in the repository README).
  Only the curated ASN list (input/datacenter/ASN.txt) is used. The repository's generated
  IP ranges, which are derived from IPLocate data under CC BY-SA 4.0, are NOT used.

- ai.robots.txt (https://github.com/ai-robots-txt/ai.robots.txt)
  Copyright (c) 2024 ai.robots.txt. MIT License.

- Tor exit list (optional): Tor Project bulk exit list
  (https://check.torproject.org/torbulkexitlist), a public list of IP addresses.
  Fallback mirror: SecOps-Institute/Tor-IP-Addresses
  (https://github.com/SecOps-Institute/Tor-IP-Addresses),
  Copyright (c) 2023 SecOps - Institute of Information Security. MIT License.

- Crawler IP ranges published by Google, Microsoft (Bing), OpenAI, Perplexity, Apple,
  Anthropic and Mistral at the URLs listed in waf-config.yaml. Used only as IP address
  lists to verify crawler identity.

